From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:38:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: zinwa-q25: reserve a camera pool

CAMSV allocates frames with dma_alloc_coherent(), which tops out at
4 MiB here: enough for a 1920x1080 frame of 16-bit samples, not for the
front IMX111's 8 MP or the rear S5KJN1's 12.5 MP frames. Reserve 256 MiB
for it below 4 GiB, CAMSV's DMA limit. The camera overlay names the pool
by phandle, so its number is fixed at 0x93, which is free in this DTB and
in the one the Q25 boots.

Tested on the Q25 with the same node added to the DTB it boots, as the
default entry: both sensors streamed full-resolution frames from the
pool.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-zinwa-q25.dts | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-zinwa-q25.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-zinwa-q25.dts
index a06ea52..3464eea 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-zinwa-q25.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-zinwa-q25.dts
@@ -92,6 +92,19 @@
 		fb_mem:       framebuffer@fe0d0000 { reg = <0 0xfe0d0000 0 0x1f2f000>; no-map; };
 		aee_lk_mem:   aee_lk@50700000      { reg = <0 0x50700000 0 0x800000>;  no-map; };
 
+		/*
+		 * Camera frames over 4 MiB. The camera overlay is applied to a DTB
+		 * without __symbols__ and names this pool by phandle.
+		 */
+		cam_pool: q25-cam-pool {
+			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+			size = <0 0x10000000>;
+			alignment = <0 0x200000>;
+			alloc-ranges = <0 0x40000000 0 0xc0000000>;
+			no-map;
+			phandle = <0x93>;
+		};
+
 	};
 
 	/*
